{"name":"Fairy Wings","hex":"#ffebf2","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"fairy","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A mythical being of human form with magical powers, known in many sizes and descriptions, although typically depicted as a small sprite with gauze-like wings, especially one that is female. Fairies are revered in some modern forms of paganism.","A male homosexual, especially one who is effeminate."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Like a fairy; fanciful, whimsical, delicate."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fairy"},{"term":"wings","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of wing"]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A type of scuba harness with an attached buoyancy compensation device: see wikipedia:Backplate and wing","A flip (hairstyle)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wings"}],"entries":[{"title":"Epimedium","blocks":[{"text":"Epimedium, also known as barrenwort, bishop's hat, fairy wings, horny goat weed, or yin yang huo, is a genus of flowering plants in the family Berberidaceae. The majority of the species are endemic to China, with smaller numbers elsewhere in Asia and a few in the Mediterranean region."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2a/Elfenblume_%28Epimedium_x_versicolor%29.jpg/330px-Elfenblume_%28Epimedium_x_versicolor%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Epimedium","wikidata":"Q157746"},{"title":"Fairy","blocks":[{"text":"A fairy is a type of mythical being or legendary creature, generally described as anthropomorphic, found in the folklore of multiple European cultures, a form of spirit, often with magical, metaphysical, supernatural, or preternatural qualities."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c5/Falero_Luis_Ricardo_Lily_Fairy_1888.jpg/330px-Falero_Luis_Ricardo_Lily_Fairy_1888.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fairy","wikidata":"Q8028"},{"title":"Wing","blocks":[{"text":"A wing is a structure which produces both lift and drag while moving through air. Wings are defined by two shape characteristics, an airfoil section and a planform. Wing efficiency is expressed as lift-to-drag ratio, which compares the benefit of lift with the air resistance of a given wing shape, as it flies. Aerodynamics includes the study of wing performance in air."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/76/Wing.two.arp.600pix.jpg/330px-Wing.two.arp.600pix.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wing","wikidata":"Q161358"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ee/Epimedium_alpinum_NRM.jpg/500px-Epimedium_alpinum_NRM.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ee/Epimedium_alpinum_NRM.jpg/1280px-Epimedium_alpinum_NRM.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ee/Epimedium_alpinum_NRM.jpg/500px-Epimedium_alpinum_NRM.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Epimedium alpinum flower; note the spurs are almost as long as the sepals","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AEpimedium_alpinum_NRM.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e3/Epimedium_%C3%97_perralchicum_%27Frohnleiten%27_in_Brest.jpg/500px-Epimedium_%C3%97_perralchicum_%27Frohnleiten%27_in_Brest.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e3/Epimedium_%C3%97_perralchicum_%27Frohnleiten%27_in_Brest.jpg/1280px-Epimedium_%C3%97_perralchicum_%27Frohnleiten%27_in_Brest.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_cam